# The files of musl (third_party/musl, vendored unmodified) that the build
# replaces with ours: musl's object for the upstream file is left out of
# libc.a and ours is compiled in its place (a header: ours is found first
# on the include path). docs/M13-PLAN.md section 1 says why each exists.
#
# One override per line: the upstream file (relative to third_party/musl),
# the SHA-256 of the upstream file our file was written against, and our
# file (relative to the top of the tree). tools/checkoverrides.py checks
# every hash before musl is built, and `make check` runs it with its
# self-test: a new musl release that changed one of these files stops the
# build until someone has read upstream's change, brought ours up to date
# and recorded the new hash here.
#
# Later tracks add theirs the same way.

